-- ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- DIGDEEP PRO DATABASE — one-paste bootstrap (generated by
-- scripts/supabase/bootstrap.sh --emit-sql; do not hand-edit, regenerate).
--
-- HOW TO USE (≈30 seconds, no credentials needed):
--   1. Supabase Dashboard → your project → SQL Editor → New query.
--   2. Paste THIS ENTIRE FILE → Run.
--   3. Done. Every statement is idempotent — re-pasting is a no-op.
--
-- WHAT THIS CREATES:
--   • The full 14-table DigDeep schema (Prisma-generated, exact match with
--     prisma/migrations).
--   • _prisma_migrations pre-seeded with the repo's real migration checksums
--     → `prisma migrate deploy` sees everything as applied (no P3009 wedge,
--     no double-apply).
--   • Hardening: ROW LEVEL SECURITY on every table + REVOKE from
--     anon/authenticated (the app connects as `postgres` = owner and is
--     unaffected; PostgREST roles get nothing).
--
-- AFTER THE PASTE: set DATABASE_URL on Vercel to the project's connection
-- string (Settings → Database → Connection string, use the Session pooler
-- URI for serverless) and redeploy. Old Vercel-Postgres data stays put.
-- ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
